not_recommended:
A JIT inside the CPython process (ORC through ctypes and libLLVM, or llvmlite). It works, but costs too much:
- a 117-123 MB libLLVM, or llvmlite 0.50.0's 56.9 MiB wheel (about 170 MiB installed, LLVM 22.1.0);
- 65 MiB RSS against 9 MiB;
- an LLJIT C API whose header says it is 'NOT stable';
- libgcc_s made visible to the JIT linker;
- 23 ms to compile, or 735 ms with the runtime as bitcode.
The AOT .so imports in about 0.4 ms and builds in 0.57 s. A compile-on-import cache (S5) gives the development loop.
